  "id": "COMPOUND:17356 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 2-[2,2-bis(1H-indol-3-yl)ethyl]aniline may interact with DNA polymerase iota through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is identified as a target of several molecules, including Oriciacridone C and rel-(7aR,13aR)-9,10-Dimethoxy-3,3-dimethyl-13,13a-dihydro-3H-pyrano[2,3-c:6,5-f']dichromen-7(7aH)-one, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. Similarly, the compound is also a target of another molecule, (+)-(8S,8'R)-4-hydroxy-5-methoxy-1',2',3',4',5',6'-hexanor-2,7'-cyclolignan-7'-one, which also targets DNA polymerase iota. These findings indicate that the compound may exert its effects on DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving the activation or inhibition of the enzyme by these downstream molecules. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where the compound acts as a modulator or inhibitor of DNA polymerase iota, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
